# Lobster dashboard API — HTTPS reverse proxy for the Oracle Cloud Linux VM.
#
# Deployed as /etc/caddy/Caddyfile on 147.15.145.250. The hostname uses
# sslip.io so Let's Encrypt can issue a certificate without owning a domain.
#
# Steps (already completed for this VM):
#   1. DNS is not needed — 147.15.145.250.sslip.io already resolves to the VM.
#   2. Caddy is installed and running as a systemd service with this file.
#      It listens on 80/443 and proxies to the bot API on 127.0.0.1:3000.
#   3. (PENDING — Oracle Cloud console) add ingress rules for TCP 80 and 443
#      in the VCN's Security List / NSG, otherwise Let's Encrypt cannot reach
#      the server and no certificate is issued.
#   4. (PENDING — Discord Developer Portal) register the redirect URI:
#        https://147.15.145.250.sslip.io/api/auth/callback
#
# If you later add a real domain, replace the hostname and set the DNS record.

147.15.145.250.sslip.io {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000
}
